<title>USA: Sysco sets 6 mln share repurchase program.</title>
<headline>Sysco sets 6 mln share repurchase program.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sysco Corp on Friday said its board of directors authorized the company to buy back up to six million shares before the end of its fiscal year ending June 1998.</p>
<p>Sysco said it bought back about nine million shares for about $305 million in the fiscal year ended June 28. It repurchased 29.4 million shares for $871 million since May 1992.</p>
<p>The distributor of food products said the buybacks had more than offset the 1 million to 2 million shares it issuesd annually for various compensation plans.</p>
<p>The company's stock closed unchanged at 37-11-16 on Friday.</p>
</text>
